&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;: 60 000€ à 70 000€ brut annuel (fixe) selon expérience et séniorité + jusqu’à 6 000€ de variable selon expérience et séniorité&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Artefact, nous sommes convaincus que la diversité des parcours, des expériences et des perspectives fait la richesse de nos équipes. Nous nous engageons à offrir un environnement inclusif et des opportunités équitables, où chacune et chacun peut évoluer et exprimer pleinement son potentiel. Nos recrutements reposent sur les compétences, le potentiel et l’adéquation avec le rôle.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;L’IA ne transforme pas une entreprise parce qu’elle est disponible, mais parce que les collaborateurs s’en emparent pour travailler autrement. Chez Artefact, nous sommes des makers : “We Make AI Work”. Notre métier n’est pas de commenter l’IA, c’est de la faire fonctionner, au cœur des métiers et à grande échelle.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Et tout commence par vous.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;En tant que Senior AI Builder, vous prenez en main un stream ou une mission bien cadrée, avec autonomie sur votre périmètre et au contact direct des clients. **Vous transmettez et construisez : vous pilotez des initiatives de montée en compétences, concevez avec les métiers des agents et solutions IA qui répondent à leurs besoins, et accompagnez leur adoption. Vous coachez les consultants juniors et êtes responsable de la qualité et des résultats de vos travaux.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Vous partez des défis des utilisateurs métiers, de leurs processus et de leurs irritants pour transformer les possibilités de l’IA en résultats tangibles. **Vous ne vous arrêtez pas au slide** : vous concevez et animez des expériences d’apprentissage qui donnent envie de passer à l’action, construisez des agents et des solutions fonctionnelles (no-code, low-code, vibe coding), et les faites évoluer au contact de leurs utilisateurs pour ancrer de nouveaux usages.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Au plus près des métiers, vous identifiez les opportunités de repenser les tâches, faire évoluer les rôles et responsabilités, et réinventer les façons de travailler avec l’IA. Vous faites le lien entre les initiatives de terrain (bottom-up) et les programmes de transformation à grande échelle (top-down), aux côtés de nos équipes AI Strategy et Engineering. Votre réussite se mesure à l’adoption réelle des solutions, à l’autonomie des équipes et aux changements concrets dans leur quotidien.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activités &amp;amp; Responsabilités&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I. Analyse &amp;amp; Cadrage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Animer des ateliers avec les métiers et le L&amp;amp;D pour analyser les besoins, segmenter les publics et cartographier un workflow.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Proposer la solution cible, le rôle de l’humain et de l’agent, les contrôles nécessaires et les critères d’acceptation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Concevoir le séquencement d’un module ou d’un parcours, avec cas d’usage, temps de pratique et modalités d’évaluation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;II. Développement &amp;amp; Déploiement des Solutions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Créer des ateliers et playbooks contextualisés, prototyper des assistants ou agents simples en amont et en direct avec les participants, à l&#39;aide de plateformes approuvées et de patterns réutilisables.Définir et exécuter jeux d&#39;essai, tests utilisateurs et critères qualité; documenter les limites et faire valider les points sensibles.Animer de manière autonome, adapter la séance au niveau du public et coacher un Junior sur ses premières animations.Traduire une question business en KPIs, en définitions et en dashboards complets livrés en autonomie, et transformer les analyses en storyline avec un « so what » clair.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;III. Adoption &amp;amp; Animation de Communauté&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Organiser office hours, challenges d&#39;application et train-the-trainer, outiller des champions et des managers de proximité.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accompagner la mise en usage, former les référents makers et préparer les supports de transfert.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Exploiter les retours des utilisateurs pendant le périmètre convenu et proposer des améliorations priorisées.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IV. Structuration et Pilotage de la démarche Change&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Suivre l&#39;adoption et la valeur du use case, les compétences acquises, la capacité à répliquer et les premiers usages; proposer des ajustements concrets pour améliorer l&#39;activation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Contribuer à l’analyse des freins et au plan de change du programme, sous la responsabilité du chef de mission.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Identifier les dépendances SI, les risques sécurité et le besoin d&#39;escalade vers la DSI ou AI Engineering.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profil recherché&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vous vous reconnaissez si… &lt;/strong&gt;vous aimez avoir la main sur un périmètre, structurer des problèmes complexes et voir vos recommandations se concrétiser, et si vous préférez mettre une démo entre les mains du client plutôt que lui décrire une vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 à 5 ans d’expérience en conseil, transformation digitale, data / IA ou conduite du changement, avec une première expérience de pilotage d’un stream ou d’une mission et de coaching de consultants juniors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une formation supérieure de niveau licence ou master, issue d’un cursus académique d’excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une bonne maîtrise de l’IA générative et agentique, et un état d’esprit de maker : capacité à concevoir et faire évoluer des agents et solutions IA fonctionnelles (no-code, low-code, vibe coding).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une aisance dans la conception et l’animation d’expériences d’apprentissage engageantes, d’ateliers collaboratifs et de dispositifs de montée en compétences par la pratique.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une capacité à comprendre les enjeux et processus métier, à embarquer les parties prenantes et à accompagner la transformation des tâches, des rôles et des pratiques de travail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une maîtrise parfaite du français et de l’anglais (oral et écrit).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;À propos d’Artefact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Artefact est un cabinet de conseil spécialisé en data et en intelligence artificielle, qui accompagne les entreprises pour transformer ces technologies en impact business concret et mesurable. À la croisée du conseil, de la data et de la technologie, nos 2 500 collaborateurs dans 27 pays mettent leurs expertises en commun pour concevoir, développer et déployer des solutions qui répondent aux enjeux de transformation de nos clients.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Notre accompagnement s&#39;étend sur l&#39;intégralité de la chaîne de valeur : &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strategize AI&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; (cadrage stratégique, opportunités à fort impact, trajectoires, modèles opérationnels), &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Deploy AI&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; (ingénierie, industrialisation, architectures agentiques, produits data) et &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Adopt AI &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;(conduite du changement, acculturation, usage quotidien de l&#39;IA).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Envie d&#39;en savoir plus ? Découvrez Artefact, nos expertises et notre culture : &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.artefact.com&quot;&gt;https://www.artefact.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi nous rejoindre?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;De la stratégie à la réalisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ne pas s’arrêter aux recommandations : participer à la conception et à la concrétisation de solutions IA répondant à de véritables enjeux métiers.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une collaboration entre expertises&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Occuper un rôle à la croisée de l&#39;humain (AI Adoption), de la stratégie (AI Strategy), de la technologie (AI Engineering).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Un rôle avec de l’autonomie et des perspectives&lt;br&gt;Piloter des streams, développer une expertise, faire grandir une équipe et contribuer au développement de l’activité.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Un parcours clair de progression&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Un accompagnement concret : counsellor, parcours de formation et programme de leadership.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processus de recrutement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;entretien de fit RH &lt;/strong&gt;(30 / 45’) avec les RH / Talent Acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;entretien de fit expert &lt;/strong&gt;(60’) avec un AI Builder Senior ou Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une &lt;strong&gt;présentation d’un cas réel &lt;/strong&gt;(60’) sur lequel le candidat a travaillé par le passé avec un Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;role play AI Adoption Senior &lt;/strong&gt;(45 / 60’) avec Directeur&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;entretien de fit final &lt;/strong&gt;(30’) avec un AI Builder Partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération &lt;/strong&gt;: 53 000€ à 63 000€ brut annuel (fixe) + jusqu’à 5 000€ de variable selon expérience et séniorité&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Artefact, nous sommes convaincus que la diversité des parcours, des expériences et des perspectives fait la richesse de nos équipes. Nous nous engageons à offrir un environnement inclusif et des opportunités équitables, où chacune et chacun peut évoluer et exprimer pleinement son potentiel. Nos recrutements reposent sur les compétences, le potentiel et l&#39;adéquation avec le rôle.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Des groupes de premier plan font tourner leur IA sur ce que vous construisez. Infrastructure cloud, plateformes de données, chaînes de delivery, serving de modèles, runtime des agents : ces fondations portent à grande échelle les applications et les agents de nos clients, et vous les concevez et les exploitez. Grâce à ce travail, les équipes produit livrent sans risque, tandis que les coûts, la latence et la sécurité restent sous contrôle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce poste est fait pour vous si vos utilisateurs sont d’autres équipes d’ingénierie et si la robustesse d’un système sous charge vous intéresse.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact accompagne les plus grandes entreprises du monde dans le déploiement de l’IA : 3 000 AI makers dans plus de 30 pays, plus de 1 000 clients. En France, le département Engineering réunit environ 300 personnes sous la responsabilité du CTO ; vous y rejoignez le chapter AI Applied Engineer, archétype Platform Engineer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activités et responsabilités&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Les Product Engineers et les AI Engineers déploient sur les plateformes que vous construisez ; leurs besoins se définissent avec eux, et leur accompagnement se poursuit jusqu’en production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sur une plateforme de données, les fondations vous reviennent : infrastructure, sécurité, réseau, calcul. Ce qui y circule relève des Context &amp;amp; Analytics Engineers. Le travail se mène aussi avec les équipes IT, sécurité et cloud du client, sous le regard desquelles chaque choix d’architecture doit pouvoir se défendre ; le code se relit entre pairs et les nouvelles recrues sont accompagnées.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos responsabilités :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Déployer l’infrastructure cloud en infrastructure as code et conduire les migrations cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Construire et exploiter des plateformes de données : entrepôts et lakehouses, orchestration, traitement batch et streaming.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Construire des pipelines CI/CD et l’outillage MLOps et LLMOps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Construire le harness des agents : runtime, frameworks d’évaluation, observabilité.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Servir les modèles et maîtriser leur coût et leur latence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Poser les fondations de sécurité : IAM, réseau, secrets, droits d’accès des agents, protection contre le prompt injection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Construire des connecteurs et des serveurs MCP que plusieurs agents réutilisent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Garantir la fiabilité : monitoring, gestion des incidents, suivi des coûts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profil recherché&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Les indispensables :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous avez construit et exploité de l’infrastructure cloud sur Google Cloud, Azure ou AWS, en infrastructure as code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Des pipelines CI/CD et des déploiements conteneurisés, par exemple sur Kubernetes, font partie de votre pratique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Les bases de la sécurité (IAM, règles réseau, gestion des secrets) s’appliquent chez vous au quotidien.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce que vous exploitez, vous le surveillez, et vous prenez part à la gestion des incidents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le code et la documentation que vous écrivez restent maintenables pour les équipes qui utilisent votre plateforme.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Les coding agents font déjà partie de votre quotidien, et vous vérifiez ce qu’ils produisent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Un plus, pas un prérequis :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une expérience de plateformes de données, par exemple sur Databricks, BigQuery ou Snowflake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une expérience MLOps ou LLMOps : serving de modèles, model registry, pipelines d’évaluation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une expérience d’observabilité d’agents ou de LLM gateway : tracing, suivi des coûts, routage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FinOps : suivi et optimisation des coûts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sécurité de l’IA : droits d’accès des agents, red teaming, guardrails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une certification cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pas besoin de cocher toutes les cases pour postuler&lt;/strong&gt; : si vous avez l’essentiel des indispensables et l’envie d’apprendre le reste, parlons-en.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi nous rejoindre ?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une plateforme n’est jamais terminée : chaque nouvel agent déployé chez un client soulève de nouvelles questions de coût, de latence et de droits d’accès. Le Platform Engineer travaille à l’endroit où ces questions se posent en premier, au plus près des équipes techniques et de sécurité du client.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous sommes des AI makers : l’IA se construit avec nos clients, pas seulement pour eux. Leurs enjeux deviennent les nôtres, et nos choix techniques s’expliquent dans le langage du métier. Les positions que nous prenons sont claires ; elles évoluent face aux faits, jamais sous la pression.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre domaine change tous les mois, et ce rythme nous convient : les nouvelles technologies et les nouveaux secteurs s’apprennent vite, et les habitudes qui ne servent plus s’abandonnent sans regret. Devant un problème difficile, le réflexe est de le découper en étapes vérifiables, avec un haut niveau d’exigence sur le code comme sur les livrables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quand il manque quelque chose, pour un client ou pour le chapter, nous le construisons. La progression passe par des retours constructifs, par le partage des connaissances, par la demande d’aide sans attendre et par la reconnaissance du travail des autres. Il y a beaucoup à apprendre, et beaucoup à construire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Un counsellor accompagne vos premiers mois. L’onboarding technique ouvre le parcours, suivi d’un premier projet client ; si aucun n’est prêt, les starter kits internes prennent le relais.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le reste s’apprend sur les projets : serving de modèles, observabilité des agents, sécurité de l’IA, avec l’appui de la communauté Platform Engineer. À partir de 2027, l’archétype Platform Engineer disposera de sa propre grille de compétences et de son propre parcours de formation, en plus du socle commun à tous les AI Applied Engineers (évaluation de l’IA, responsabilité en production).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une spécialisation en sécurité de l’IA (red teaming, guardrails, conformité à l’AI Act) est possible : elle relève aujourd’hui de l’archétype Platform Engineer. Plus tard, un rôle transverse s’ouvre (Project Tech Lead, Pre-sales Engineer, Engineering Manager), et les Platform Engineers seniors peuvent rejoindre le chapter AI Architect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processus de recrutement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le processus demande environ quatre heures, réparties en six étapes dont une seule sur site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entretien RH&lt;/strong&gt; (45 min, à distance) : parcours, motivations et points pratiques, comme le calendrier et les prétentions salariales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Appel avec le CTO&lt;/strong&gt; (15 à 30 min, à distance).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Screening technique&lt;/strong&gt; (30 min, à distance, avec un membre du chapter AI Applied Engineer) : retour détaillé sur vos projets passés, puis questions techniques et de design de solution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code review et live coding&lt;/strong&gt; (60 min, sur site, avec un membre du chapter) : relecture d’un dépôt de code existant et correction de ses défauts, puis construction d’une nouvelle fonctionnalité avec un coding agent et présentation du résultat.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cas technique&lt;/strong&gt; (45 min, à distance, avec un membre du chapter) : cadrage d’un problème métier, proposition d’une solution technique, description de la méthode d’évaluation, puis discussion de vos choix.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Entretien final&lt;/strong&gt; (30 min, à distance, avec une personne de l’encadrement du département, Engineering Manager ou Director) : reprise des points restés ouverts, choix de l’archétype et du niveau les mieux adaptés à votre profil, et réponses à toutes vos questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Selon les étapes, tous les outils d’IA sont autorisés, ou aucun. Lors du live coding, c’est la manière de travailler avec l’assistance de l’IA qui est observée.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;: 75 000€ à 85 000€ brut annuel (fixe) + jusqu’à 8 000€ de variable selon expérience et séniorité&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Artefact, nous sommes convaincus que la diversité des parcours, des expériences et des perspectives fait la richesse de nos équipes. Nous nous engageons à offrir un environnement inclusif et des opportunités équitables, où chacune et chacun peut évoluer et exprimer pleinement son potentiel. Nos recrutements reposent sur les compétences, le potentiel et l’adéquation avec le rôle.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Autonomous Drone Software Engineer to join a swarming programme. As an engineer on a lean, high-impact team, you will have the opportunity to drive development of new features, have a say in architecture and design decisions and have real impact across all the team’s projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will not be siloed; this role spans the entire autonomy lifecycle, from developing autonomy capabilities to investigating real-world flight-test data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who’s a self-starter, can work independently, can work with ambiguity, can take decisions on their own and not be afraid to drive and push towards getting the project across the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership and drive the development of new features across the autonomy stack and partner integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with hardware engineers, product managers, and external partners to define system requirements and translate them into robust software architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement robust distributed state machines, leader election protocols, and fault-tolerant architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clean, readable and maintainable code while confidently managing complex concurrency and contention scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and run rigorous tests utilizing SITL/HITL simulation environments to validate code prior to physical deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in code reviews, architectural discussions, and technical documentation to elevate the team&#39;s engineering standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act decisively during flight-test investigations, applying strong engineering judgment to physical failure modes and release safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional engineering experience in robotics, embedded systems, or distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep proficiency in modern C++, with practical experience designing, reasoning about, and debugging highly concurrent systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded systems experience working close to hardware on real-time or safety-critical platforms (e.g., avionics, automotive, robotics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong architectural understanding of distributed systems, with the ability to deliberately evaluate and select consensus designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with robust release management, versioned artifacts, and pinned dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4, MAVLink, and related drone software ecosystems is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CoLab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoLab, we help mechanical engineering teams bring life-changing products to market years sooner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build AI for engineers designing cars, medical devices, and jet engines. Products this complex aren&#39;t sketched and sent to production. Teams spend months on iterations, reviews, and tests, predicting how every part performs before anything is built. CoLab is where those reviews happen, and we capture the rationale behind every change. Other tools show what changed between versions. Only CoLab knows why. That&#39;s how our AI helps manufacturers like Bobcat, Triumph Motorcycles, and GE Appliances make better decisions, eliminate rework cycles, and get to market faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proudly based in St. John’s, Newfoundland, CoLab started with one customer in 2018. Since then we’ve raised a&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/ai-is-changing-engineering-colab-just-raised-72m-to-lead-the-transformation&quot;&gt; $72M Series C&lt;/a&gt;, been named the 57th fastest growing company in North America by Deloitte (&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/colab-ranked-number-57-fastest-growing-company-in-north-america-on-the-2025-deloitte-technology-fast-500&quot;&gt;Fast 500™&lt;/a&gt;), signed multi-year&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-bombardier-signs-contract-colab-ai-software/&quot;&gt; AI partnerships with companies like Bombardier&lt;/a&gt;, and grown to a team of 250+.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role that helps define how CoLab delivers technical value to its most strategic customers in Aerospace and Defence. CoLab is a category-creating product, which means adoption isn&#39;t just a rollout. It&#39;s a change in how the organization works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;d act as a trusted advisor, leveraging people, process, and technology to help teams rethink how they manage feedback, data, and decision-making across design and PLM. That means getting deep into customer workflows, testing new ways of working, and building repeatable methods the rest of the team can scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside a Customer Success Manager, and use what you learn on the front line to help shape product direction. This role isn&#39;t about selling or pitching. It&#39;s about deeply understanding engineering problems and solving them alongside the customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a candidate in Switzerland to work regularly on-site with local CoLab customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Ideal Candidate&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a mechanical engineer by trade and have worked as a designer in an A&amp;amp;D company. You also understand the full product development life cycle: how design, manufacturing, quality, and engineering leadership depend on each other, and where collaboration breaks down. You can coach those teams toward working together better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You know how to improve that life cycle with technology. Maybe you’ve championed internal tools or created automation or scripts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You also know a process that makes sense on paper won’t get adopted on its own. You can meet people where they are, including the stakeholders who don’t want to change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need to be the loudest voice in the room, but you can run a sprint and lead a cross-functional project. If the average person might find this job too undefined or complex, that probably excites you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mapping a customer&#39;s current-state design review and engineering workflows, and defining the target-state process their teams will actually adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploying and tuning CoLab&#39;s AI capabilities against a customer&#39;s own standards, drawing checklists, and design guidelines, and diagnosing what&#39;s working and what isn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing mechanical engineering expertise to validate AI-generated results and ensure engineering rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating and solving complex engineering data and integration challenges across PLM, ERP, QMS, and traditional design feedback tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expanding adoption into new teams, programs, and sites within the account, partnering with the Customer Success Manager on where the next opportunity sits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with product teams to identify feature gaps, improve capabilities, and refine AutoReview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in mechanical design engineering, ideally in a medium- to large-sized organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of PLM &amp;amp; ERP systems and enterprise engineering data architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead technical projects and cross-functional collaborations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with customers or internal stakeholders to solve technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in fast-changing, ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication and documentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of high-level AI architecture, specifically LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs, data integrations, and enterprise architecture concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in Switzerland&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with internal tool development, scripting, or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AI/ML tools applied to engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in design consulting or product development at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this is a fully remote role, travel is a consistent part of the job. There are two primary types of travel you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Weeks:&lt;/strong&gt; Once per quarter, the sales team or entire company gets together in person. These typically involve traveling out on a Monday and returning on a Thursday or Friday. Two of these each year are held at our headquarters in St. John&#39;s, Newfoundland, Canada and the others take place in more central locations that evolve as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-sites:&lt;/strong&gt; This role will work closely with a local customer with expectations to be on site with that customer, so there will likely be far less travel than our typical MFDE roll. That being said, in the event the local customer were to no longer work with us, the following is our standard MFDE travel expectations: “For most of our large deployment customers, we will visit on-site during kick-off and key expansion opportunities. Most on-sites involve 2-3 days with the customer, with travel on either side. Travel is primarily within North America, and you can expect 4 customer on-sites per quarter.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Extra Details&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a full-time, permanent position with a competitive compensation package that includes stock options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited paid vacation and extended health benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equity Note&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Frequently cited statistics show that people who identify with historically marginalized groups are likely to apply to jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. We encourage you to help us break that statistic and apply even if you don&#39;t meet every single qualification. Your potential is what matters most to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;IonQ is hiring a Senior Quantum Sales Director to drive new and expansion revenue for Capella Data as a Service (DaaS) and satellite systems across EMEA. You will own a portfolio of strategic enterprise, defence and government accounts, selling SAR imagery and analytics subscriptions, tasking capacity and complete satellite systems, and you will report to Garrick Ballantine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a quota carrying, hunter oriented role for a seller who can run long cycle capital programmes alongside faster moving data subscriptions, and who can translate space based sensing into mission and business outcomes. The role is remote, employed through an IonQ entity in the UK (Oxford) or Switzerland, with travel of up to 20%.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own an annual new business and expansion quota across Capella DaaS subscriptions, tasking capacity and satellite system sales within an assigned enterprise, defence and civil government territory in EMEA. You will build and execute account plans for a named portfolio, mapping stakeholders across mission, programme, procurement and technical functions and building executive relationships at several levels in each account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will sell the full value chain, from SAR data and analytics subscriptions and recurring tasking commitments to ground segment integration and dedicated or jointly owned satellite systems. Working with product, engineering and mission solutions teams, you will bring customer requirements back into the roadmap and represent IonQ at industry, defence and geospatial conferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run complex, consultative sales cycles from prospecting through to close, including discovery, technical validation with solutions engineering, pricing, contracting and negotiation of subscription and system purchase agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to RFIs, RFPs and government tenders in partnership with capture, proposal and contracts teams, and support prime and subcontractor teaming strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast accurately in CRM, keep disciplined pipeline hygiene and deliver reliable monthly and quarterly commits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive relationships across mission, programme, procurement and technical stakeholders in each account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent IonQ at industry, defence and geospatial events across EMEA, and feed customer requirements back to product and engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will bring substantial enterprise sales experience in geospatial data, earth observation, satellite systems, defence technology or adjacent data and SaaS markets, with a consistent record of exceeding quota. You will have closed both recurring data or subscription contracts and large capital or programme based hardware sales, and you will have sold to EMEA and allied government, defence and security customers, with a working knowledge of their procurement frameworks and contracting cycles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have command of a structured sales methodology such as MEDDICC or Challenger, with disciplined CRM and forecasting rigour, and the ability to engage credibly with technical and mission stakeholders on remote sensing, SAR, tasking and data delivery workflows. A bachelor&#39;s degree in business, engineering or a related field, and willingness to travel up to 20%, are also required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You’d be a great fit with:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience selling SAR, optical imagery or RF sensing data and analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in satellite systems, ground segment or space mission integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in early market development or category creation for an emerging technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to obtain the relevant national security clearance in your country of employment, such as UK SC or NATO clearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established relationships with EMEA government, defence or security customers, including NATO and allied programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package includes base salary, bonus, equity, and a range of benefits available on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive at Ripple Treasury, you will play a key role in our sales team, driving success in a high-growth region. This position offers an outstanding opportunity to work with a world-class team. You will help develop the future of corporate treasury by integrating modern technology with proven financial solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibility is to exclusively win new corporate clients for Ripple Treasury. This role requires effective positioning of a curated selection of the Ripple Treasury Platform&#39;s core capabilities to each target account, with end-to-end accountability for territory development and full deal lifecycle management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve new business revenue goals set forth by Managing Director of Europe Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win corporate new accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop pipeline consistently across your territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend trade shows, industry events, and user events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a deep understanding of your market and its evolving potential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse and understand sales growth potential in your assigned territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed about the treasury industry and competition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with your manager and sales team to develop competitive strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a minimum of 10 days monthly in-office presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in New Business SaaS Sales, preferably in enterprise FinTech/Treasury Management Systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated large account navigation and complex sales cycle management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to position functionally rich, sophisticated value propositions across multiple business areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to execute pipeline generation at scale through outbound, driving and maintaining a 4x pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent track record of top sales performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent value based, consultative selling skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven organizational and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel 25-50%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in business or equivalent experience preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Do Your Best Work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The opportunity to build in a fast-paced start-up environment with experienced industry leaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A learning environment where you can dive deep into the latest technologies and make an impact.&amp;nbsp; A professional development budget to support other modes of learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Thrive in an environment where no matter what race, ethnicity, gender, origin, or culture they identify with, every employee is a respected, valued, and empowered part of the team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In-office collaboration for moments that matter is important to our culture, and we give managers and teams the flexibility to decide which 10+ days a month they come in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bi-weekly all-company meeting - business updates and ask me anything style discussion with our Leadership Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We come together for moments that matter which include team offsites, team bonding activities, happy hours and more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Control of Your Finances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonuses, and equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive benefits that cover physical and mental healthcare, retirement, family forming, and family support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee giving match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mobile phone stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Care of Yourself&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;R&amp;amp;R days so you can rest and recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous wellness reimbursement and weekly onsite &amp;amp; virtual programming&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous vacation policy - work with your manager to take time off when you need it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Industry-leading parental leave policies. Family planning benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Catered lunches, fully-stocked kitchens with premium snacks/beverages, and plenty of fun events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Benefits listed above are for full-time employees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ripple is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We’re committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We do not discriminate against qualified employees or applicants because of race, color, religion, gender identity, sex, sexual identity, pregnancy, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, military status, or any other characteristic protected by local law or ordinance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please find our California, UK/EU, Singapore, DIFC, ADGM, Australia, and Switzerland&amp;nbsp; &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;for reference.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Garda Capital Partners (Garda) is a multi-billion dollar alternative investment firm with over 22 years of experience deploying relative value strategies across fixed income markets for institutional investors. We hire, grow, and mentor great talent and remain steadfast in our commitment to building a culture that helps them succeed. Garda is more than a workplace. We are built on trust, integrity, and a shared vision for how we work together, the enduring relationships we build, and the consistency of our results. Garda&#39;s primary offices are located in Wayzata, New York City, West Palm Beach, Geneva, Zug, Copenhagen, Singapore, and Scottsdale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Garda is seeking an Infrastructure Engineer to own Platform Engineering &amp;amp; Automation. This hands-on role builds and operates shared deployment capabilities for infrastructure and selected applications, while providing advanced infrastructure engineering and production support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The engineer develops reusable deployment pipelines, infrastructure templates, and self-service workflows that help teams provision environments and release changes consistently — working with architecture, application owners, and regional teams to improve platform reliability and resolve complex infrastructure problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Escalation &amp;amp; Infrastructure Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior escalation point for complex infrastructure incidents and recurring operational problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot across Windows/Linux systems, identity, networking, cloud, virtualization, storage, and backup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root-cause analysis and convert recurring incidents into engineering work or documented standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in major changes, recovery events, and follow-the-sun handoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Platform Engineering &amp;amp; Deployment Automation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automation using PowerShell, Python, and APIs with production-quality testing and error handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own reusable infrastructure-as-code and configuration templates (Terraform, Ansible)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate CI/CD pipelines for infrastructure and applications, including validation, environment promotion, health checks, and rollback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply Git, peer review, automated tests, change controls, and secure secrets handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Observability, Reliability &amp;amp; Standards&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve monitoring, logging, metrics, dashboards, alerting, and automated health checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tune operational signals to reduce noise and improve detection/recovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain reusable provisioning workflows and self-service capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own platform reliability and lifecycle improvements with service owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and workplace technology staff in troubleshooting and automation practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review infrastructure code and pipeline designs with architecture, Security, and application owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain runbooks, diagrams, and onboarding guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a prioritized platform backlog with the architect and regional leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Desired Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–6 years of hands-on infrastructure operations experience across several domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in IT, computer science, computer engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced PowerShell or Python automation experience, including API integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with infrastructure as code or configuration management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and supporting CI/CD pipelines (Git, testing, secure deployment, rollback)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting, root-cause analysis, and incident-response skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of monitoring, logging, alerting, and observability concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to document work, mentor others, and collaborate across a distributed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preference for experience with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS, container platforms, modern cloud operating patterns (Azure a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering reusable provisioning workflows for infrastructure and business applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ITSM, change, incident, and problem-management practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial services or another performance-sensitive environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of solving complex infrastructure problems and building shared capabilities other teams can use independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of maintaining high standards for reliability, documentation, and maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience remaining effective under pressure, with a history of mentoring and knowledge-sharing within teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.gardacp.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Candidate_Privacy_Notice.pdf&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snr Director West International Cluster, &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Rare BU - Closing Date: November 13, 2027.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be responsible to develop and execute all sales and marketing activities in the relative cluster of countries, with immediate focus on driving the development of GIVLAARI and OXLUMO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and challenge regional and local teams in tailoring the global strategy to the specific markets while maintaining global/regional alignment;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allocate investment and drive and track focused execution of cross-functional tactics;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share learnings and best practices across the Global Rare Business Unit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will lead a team of &amp;nbsp;Field Business Leaders (FBL) across a group of geographies and be the primary interface with local Country Managers and International TTR BU shared services (eg Regional Commercial, Business Operations and and Market Access). They will appropriately partner with Medical and Regional Marketing to ensure optimal alignment, insight sharing and communication. &amp;nbsp;The Cluster Head will also build and execute the Cluster tactical plan (e.g.,Sales force and HCP target group prioritization,&amp;nbsp; congress activities, marketing materials) and participate in the regional tactics as appropriate (e.g., European congresses).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Cluster Head reports to the VP, International Rare Head.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Manages the full Commercial Team for the specific geographies (Field Business Leaders and their KAMs)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize the commercial potential of Alnylam’s assets through the development and implementation of strategic/operational plans in close collaboration with Global Rare marketing, Medical Affairs and Market Access teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, plan and set the commercial direction for the business within the Cluster, utilizing innovative techniques to drive increased customer value and market penetration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the cross-functional team providing vision, motivation, and support and coaching infrastructure to drive the business and achieve portfolio objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Market Access and Country Managers to identify, develop, propose and execute local reimbursement plans, including alignment with appropriate adaptation of European pricing, reimbursement and access strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively lead and build a high performing commercial team by hiring top talent, addressing talent gaps, upskilling and providing career guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take responsibility and accountability to deliver against the agreed commercial and strategic objectives, as well as Quality, Compliance and risk management in the countries of the cluster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that all business activities are in line with company policies, procedures and local guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds sustainable relationships with local healthcare stakeholders, functions as main partner for local customers and local/ international KOLs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure high quality revenue and volume forecasting and brand investment deployment for the cluster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops and implements innovative, multichannel marketing strategies and tactics in the cluster, including the planning and tracking of commercial spent investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In close collaboration with the Global marketing teams, ensure deep local market and stakeholder insights to inform local tailoring of the strategy and tactics and to help inform the global/regional strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributes to the development of the Global strategic plan and annual tactical plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure detailed pre-launch and post-launch tracking of agreed KPIs to allow early course correction and ensure execution of key tactics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications, Key Skills, and Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Science degree or Business degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge / experience of working in a bio/pharmaceutical commercial (Sales &amp;amp; Marketing) team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in collaboration in Cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable commercial leadership experience in the biopharmaceutical industry such as a highly successful Sales Manager or Marketing Manager and a strong sales &amp;amp; marketing leader within the specialty therapeutics arena, orphan drugs is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a track record of successful budget management with an understanding of revenue forecasting and expense budget planning and tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have the ability to build and drive a business, whilst possessing innate ‘market-making’ capabilities with natural self-starter, hands-on, entrepreneurial and innovative attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership qualities such as having the ability to attract, motive and retain talent and drive a culture of collaboration, engagement and motivation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide strategic input at Global level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding knowledge of the Rare Disease space, including Market Access key success factors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong network/matrix stakeholder communications skills with both regional and in-country teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business and financial acumen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relentless external customer and patient focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding strategic thinking combined with strong execution leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspirational leader, able to energize and motivate cross-functional teams and Sales Force&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous working style, pragmatic and operationally oriented, excellent planning and organizing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sense of urgency, ethics and responsibility&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent command of written and spoken English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to travel approximately is required - 60% domestically and some internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Alnylam:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Alnylam Pharmaceuticals (Nasdaq: ALNY) has led the translation of RNA interference (RNAi) into a whole new class of innovative medicines with the potential to transform the lives of people afflicted with rare and more prevalent diseases. Based on Nobel Prize-winning science, RNAi therapeutics represent a powerful, clinically validated approach to treating diseases at their genetic source by “interfering” with mRNA that cause or contribute to disease. Since our founding in 2002, Alnylam has led the RNAi Revolution and continues to turn scientific possibility into reality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our culture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Our people-first culture is guided by our core values: fiercely innovative, open culture, purposeful urgency, passion for excellence, and commitment to people, and these values influence how we work and the business decisions we make. Thanks to feedback from our employees over the years, we’ve been fortunate to be named a top employer around the world. Alnylam is extremely proud to have been recognized as one of Science Magazine’s Top Biopharma Employers, one of America&#39;s Most Responsible Companies for 2024 by Newsweek, a Fast Company Best Workplace for Innovators, and a Great Place to Work in Canada, France, Italy, Spain, Switzerland, and UK – among others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alnylam, we commit to an inclusive recruitment process and equal employment opportunity. We are dedicated to building an environment where employees can feel that they belong, can bring their authentic selves to work, and achieve to their full potential. By empowering employees to embrace their unique differences at work, our business grows stronger with advanced and original thinking, allowing us to bring groundbreaking medicines to patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before applying, please review Alnylam&#39;s ⁠Candidate&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://alnylampolicies.com/&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; regarding how Alnylam handles Personal Data you provide with your application for employment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-CC1&amp;nbsp;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Flexport:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Flexport, we believe global trade can move the human race forward. That’s why it’s our mission to make global commerce so easy there will be more of it. We’re shaping the future of a $10T industry with solutions powered by innovative technology and exceptional people. Today, companies of all sizes—from emerging brands to Fortune 500s—use Flexport technology to move more than $19B of merchandise across 112 countries a year.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recent global supply chain crisis has put Flexport center stage as we continue to play a pivotal role in how goods move around the world. We are proud to have the support of the best investors in the game who believe in our mission, solutions and people. Ready to tackle global challenges that impact business, society, and the environment? Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and grow with us! Join Flexport Switzerland as a Founding Account Executive&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;This is the first Account Executive position on the ground in Switzerland, Flexport’s newest market. As part of the founding commercial team, you’ll build the territory from the ground up: shaping the go-to-market approach, establishing our first customer relationships, and defining how Flexport operates and wins in the Swiss market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll drive complex, high-value deals and build long-term strategic partnerships with medium-sized and large customers. These are multi-stakeholder sales cycles that often span regions, business units, decision layers and require the ability to translate solutions into value&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll operate with a high degree of autonomy, shaping deal strategy, influencing executive stakeholders, and orchestrating cross-functional teams to deliver differentiated, value-driven solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Build pipeline and dive deep into the market&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strategic pipeline through your own prospecting, account planning, and in close collaboration with our SDR team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Flexport at industry events, associations and networks to build the brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share market insight and customer feedback with leadership, and help shape the Swiss sales playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Win new business&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle, from first meeting to signed contract, and meet or exceed quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery with senior stakeholders in logistics, procurement, finance, IT, and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design integrated, multi-product Flexport solutions aligned to customer priorities and backed by clear business cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead pricing, negotiation, and contracting, bringing in Ops, Finance, Legal, and Product as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep forecasts and pipeline accurate in Salesforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Launch and grow customers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own onboarding so new customers ramp smoothly and become our Swiss references.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build long-term relationships with senior customer stakeholders and hand accounts over smoothly to Account Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to deal reviews, sales best practices, and peer coaching across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of B2B sales closing complex deals with several decision-makers, with consistent quota attainment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logistics, freight forwarding or supply chain experience, combined with tech sales acumen: you can sell a platform as confidently as a freight service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of the Swiss market and local business landscape, with the credibility to engage senior buyers from day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who ramps fast, stays curious and does well with ambiguity and no established playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence, plus value-based discovery and negotiation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent German and English; French and/or Italian are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An opportunity to contribute to one of the fastest-growing companies, where you’ll have the chance to create a global impact while being part of a thriving multinational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity program: every team member becomes a shareholder, aligning our success with yours. As a private company in a multi-trillion-dollar industry, you have a direct stake in our collective growth and success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Program through Aetna Resources for Living: Flexport provides an employer-sponsored program at no cost to you and your household members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental leave benefit: Flexport is here to support you and your family in one of the most important times in life, the birth of a child. Our parental leave program allows both mothers and partners to take time off from work for pregnancy, childbirth, and to bond with your new child.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; At Flexport, our ability to fulfill our mission of making global commerce easy and accessible relies on having a diverse, dedicated and engaged workforce. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, physical and mental disability, health status, marital and family status, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, military and veteran status, and any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
