&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPANY OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is a leading global investment firm that offers alternative asset management as well as capital markets and insurance solutions. KKR aims to generate attractive investment returns by following a patient and disciplined investment approach, employing world-class people, and supporting growth in its portfolio companies and communities. KKR sponsors investment funds that invest in private equity, credit and real assets and has strategic partners that manage hedge funds. KKR’s insurance subsidiaries offer retirement, life and reinsurance products under the management of Global Atlantic Financial Group. References to KKR’s investments may include the activities of its sponsored funds and insurance subsidiaries.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TEAM OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR’s Public Policy &amp;amp; Affairs (PPA) function is responsible for shaping and executing the firm’s global public policy, regulatory, and external engagement strategy. The team includes regional policy teams across the Americas, EMEA, and Asia-Pacific. PPA plays a critical role in protecting and enhancing KKR’s “license to operate” by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipating regulatory and geopolitical developments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising investment teams on policy-related risks and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting portfolio companies in navigating complex stakeholder environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging with governments, regulators, and industry bodies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team operates at the intersection of investing, policy, and reputation directly contributing to investment outcomes and long-term value creation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POSITION SUMMARY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR is seeking an Principal to join its EMEA Public Policy &amp;amp; Affairs team, based in London and working directly with &amp;nbsp;the Head of EMEA Public Policy &amp;amp; Affairs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This opportunity is for a public policy and affairs professional who combines strategic judgement with strong execution capabilities. Working closely with the Head of EMEA Public Policy &amp;amp; Affairs, you will play a key role in translating the firm’s strategic priorities into concrete action and ensuring that political and regulatory insights inform investment decisions and portfolio company strategies. The role requires someone who can operate independently, manage complex and competing priorities, coordinate effectively across investment teams and internal stakeholders, and drive initiatives from analysis through execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and assess legislative, regulatory and geopolitical developments across EMEA, identifying emerging risks and opportunities for KKR and its portfolio companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a forward-looking perspective on policy and geopolitical trends, translating complex developments into actionable insights for investment teams and senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with investment teams to integrate policy and geopolitical considerations into investment theses, due diligence and decision-making, including assessments of regulatory, political, reputational and stakeholder risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the preparation and coordination of senior executive and C-suite engagements, including high-quality briefings, strategic messaging and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support portfolio companies on regulatory positioning, government relations and market-specific policy challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute targeted stakeholder engagement strategies across priority EMEA markets, including through relevant industry associations and trade bodies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support initiatives that reinforce KKR&#39;s reputation as a provider of trusted, long-term capital.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to EMEA Public Policy &amp;amp; Affairs thought leadership, internal strategic initiatives and fundraising activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over time, take ownership of key EMEA Public Policy &amp;amp; Affairs workstreams, driving priorities from strategic analysis through to execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REQUIREMENTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least six years of relevant experience in public policy, government affairs, consulting, financial services or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of EMEA political, regulatory and geopolitical dynamics, ideally with experience across multiple jurisdictions and firsthand exposure to policymaking processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global organisation, with familiarity with both European and US policy environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound commercial judgement and an understanding of how political and regulatory developments affect investment decisions, portfolio performance and business strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to anticipate emerging policy risks and opportunities, connect complex developments to commercial priorities and formulate actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to independently manage complex workstreams, balance competing priorities and deliver high-quality outcomes in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to synthesise complex information into clear, concise and decision-oriented insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare executive-level briefings and strategic materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Credibility, judgement and confidence to work effectively with senior leadership, investment professionals and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaborative skills and the ability to navigate a global, matrixed organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, intellectually curious and comfortable operating at both strategic and operational levels, with a hands-on approach to execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-ONSITE&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;KKR is an equal opportunity employer.&amp;nbsp; Individuals seeking employment are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, or any other category protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;KKR will provide reasonable accommodations as required by applicable federal, state, and/or local laws. Individuals seeking an accommodation for the application or interview process should email&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- Emails sent for unrelated issues, such as following up on an application, will not receive a response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are a qualified individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, you may request a reasonable accommodation if you are unable or limited in your ability to use or access&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kkr.com/careers&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.kkr.com/careers&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1774021690220000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1AG2WRszai8PfCsE-FH5EJ&quot;&gt;https://www.kkr.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;because of your disability. You can request reasonable accommodations by sending an email to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- Only emails left for this purpose will be returned.&lt;/p&gt;
