&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The EMEA Field Engineering organization is the technical engine of CoreWeave’s regional go-to-market. It brings together account-aligned technical teams and deep specialists to help customers design, validate, deploy, and scale production workloads on CoreWeave’s AI Cloud platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role: &lt;/strong&gt;The Senior Director of Product &amp;amp; Engineering, EMEA reports to the VP and Managing Director of EMEA, with a matrix reporting line to the Global VP of Field Engineering and SVP of Product. As the senior field technology leader for the region, you will lead all EMEA field technical functions, with direct management accountability for account-aligned technical teams and matrix leadership of specialist teams. You will set the regional technical strategy, build a consistently high level of mastery across the specialisms required to serve AI infrastructure customers, and ensure teams are motivated, appropriately deployed, and equipped to succeed. Working across EMEA and global leadership, you will turn customer and business priorities into a disciplined technical operating model that accelerates adoption, expansion, and measurable value from CoreWeave’s AI Cloud platform. You will be responsible for ensuring the product strategy of CoreWeave is assimilated across field teams in EMEA and - working with field enablement - ensuring that all teams maintain a high level of product competency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the EMEA Field Product &amp;amp; Engineering strategy, operating model, and priorities in partnership with the VP and Managing Director of EMEA, Global VP of Field Engineering and SVP of Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the senior field technology voice for EMEA, shaping go-to-market priorities, customer engagement models, technical positioning, and regional investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the account-aligned technical organization with direct accountability for organization design, performance, coaching, succession, hiring, retention, and leadership development across EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide matrix leadership to specialist technical teams, aligning priorities, coverage, engagement standards, and accountability while partnering effectively with their global functional leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a measurable technical mastery system—including skills assessments, learning plans, communities of practice, playbooks, reference architectures, and proof frameworks—that keeps teams current across AI infrastructure, compute, Kubernetes, networking, storage, security, observability, and AI/ML workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create repeatable engagement mechanisms that move customers from discovery and architecture through validation, onboarding, production readiness, adoption, optimization, and expansion on CoreWeave’s AI Cloud platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as executive technical sponsor and escalation leader for strategic customers, advising C-suite and senior technical stakeholders and mobilizing field, specialist, Product, Engineering, Support, and Operations resources around successful outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with EMEA sales leadership on account strategy, technical qualification, executive alignment, and resource allocation, sharing accountability for technical win rate, qualified pipeline, deal velocity, time to production, workload adoption, and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a rigorous regional operating cadence covering goals, metrics, forecasting, capacity and coverage planning, business reviews, and annual planning so performance and investment choices are visible and evidence based.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a structured feedback loop from EMEA customers and field teams into Product and Engineering, translating recurring requirements, adoption blockers, competitive signals, and market dynamics into clear roadmap input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent CoreWeave’s technology vision through executive briefings, customer forums, conferences, and thought leadership, while bringing relevant market insight back into the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent EMEA in global Field Engineering leadership, scale regional best practices across the company, and create an inclusive, high-performance environment in which teams are motivated and enabled to help customers adopt CoreWeave.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in technical design, implementation, consulting, pre-sales, solutions architecture, or another customer-facing technical discipline within cloud infrastructure, AI/ML platforms, enterprise software, or adjacent markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of technical leadership experience, including 7+ years leading managers, senior individual contributors, or multi-country Field Engineering, Solutions Architecture, Sales Engineering, or comparable customer-facing technical organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of leading distributed technical organizations through rapid growth, transformation, changing market conditions, and complex organizational dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical credibility in cloud-native and distributed-systems architecture, with depth across several of the following domains: accelerated compute, Kubernetes, networking, storage, security, observability, data platforms, or AI/ML workload architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success guiding complex enterprise customers from strategy and solution design through validation, production deployment, operationalization, measurable adoption, and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising C-suite and senior technical stakeholders and translating complex architecture into business value, investment choices, delivery risk, and operating decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting complex enterprise sales cycles and connecting technical strategy to qualified pipeline, technical wins, deal progression, customer adoption, and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of hiring, developing, and retaining technical leaders, together with building measurable enablement, accreditation, or continuous-learning programs that close capability gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating a metrics-based field organization, including goals, forecasting, capacity and coverage planning, resource prioritization, business reviews, and performance inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to align Sales, Customer Success, Product, Engineering, Support, Operations, partners, specialist teams, and global leaders without relying solely on positional authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across EMEA markets, with the ability to travel regionally and internationally as required to support customers, teams, and company priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership experience in a high-growth AI cloud, hyperscale cloud, data-center infrastructure, enterprise platform, or developer-platform business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with GPU-accelerated computing, large-scale AI training or inference, high-performance computing, and the operational requirements of distributed AI workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating EMEA-specific customer requirements, including data sovereignty, security, regulation, procurement, and cross-border operating considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing specialist communities of practice or centers of excellence, influencing product roadmaps, and representing a company through external technical thought leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in computer science, engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience; postgraduate technical or business study is valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit? We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You love building technical leaders and teams that combine deep expertise, commercial awareness, and a relentless focus on customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about the fast-moving AI infrastructure landscape and turn new learning and customer insight into practical enablement and better products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an expert at creating clarity, accountability, and momentum across direct and matrixed organizations operating at high speed and across cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast!&amp;nbsp; We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;CoreWeave does not accept speculative CVs. Any unsolicited CVs received will be treated as the property of CoreWeave and your Terms &amp;amp; Conditions associated with the use of CVs will be considered null and void.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Any unsolicited CVs sent by your company to us – that is to say, in any situation where we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy – will be considered by us to be a “free gift”, leaving us liable for no fees whatsoever should we choose to contact the candidate directly and engage the candidate’s services, and will in no way establish any prior claim by your company to representation of that candidate should the candidate’s details also be submitted by any other party.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires access to export controlled information. &amp;nbsp;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations applicable to that information, applicant must either be (A) a U.S. person, defined as a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful permanent resident (green card holder), (iii) refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, (B) eligible to access the export controlled information without a required export authorization, or (C) eligible and reasonably likely to obtain the required export authorization from the applicable U.S. government agency. &amp;nbsp;CoreWeave may, for legitimate business reasons, decline to pursue any export licensing process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Updated privacy notice - UK and EU Job Applications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected by CoreWeave UK Ltd. (“Controller”), which is located at&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Phosphor (6th Floor), 133 Park Street, London, SE1 9EA&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;and can be contacted by emailing ----- Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at ----- Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of (i) Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) and (ii) the GDPR as it forms part of the laws of the UK (“UK GDPR”), as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment. Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. With respect to transfers originating from the UK or the European Economic Area (&quot;EEA&quot;) to a country outside the UK or the EEA, we implement the appropriate transfer mechanism(s) and other appropriate solutions to address cross-border transfers as required by applicable law. You may request a copy of the suitable mechanisms we have in place by contacting us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. Where permitted by applicable law, we may also retain your personal data for a limited period after the recruitment process ends in order to consider you for future job opportunities, respond to legal claims, or comply with record-keeping obligations. Under the GDPR and the UK GDPR, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability. In addition, you may lodge a complaint with the relevant supervisory authority: (i) A list of Europe’s data protection authorities can be found &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/structure/data-protection-authorities/index_en.htm__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9xVQGfFw$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;; and (ii) for the UK, this is the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ico.org.uk/__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9IDhJOUA$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Information Commissioner&#39;s Office&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For additional information, please see our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.coreweave.com/docs/policies/terms-of-service/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_quote&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_-113912706363268805m_-2746164444908759431gmail-docs-internal-guid-131e4fb0-7fff-b4e9-ff50-e8cf32449b1b&quot;&gt;CoreWeave is The Essential Cloud for AI™. Built for pioneers by pioneers, CoreWeave delivers a platform of technology, tools, and teams that enables innovators to build and scale AI with confidence. Trusted by leading AI labs, startups, and global enterprises, CoreWeave combines superior infrastructure performance with deep technical expertise to accelerate breakthroughs and turn compute into capability. Founded in 2017, CoreWeave became a publicly traded company (Nasdaq: CRWV) in March 2025. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coreweave.com&quot;&gt;www.coreweave.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re proud to be a Living Wage accredited Employer.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Global Field Marketing Organization&lt;/strong&gt; drives market penetration, customer engagement, and pipeline generation across key regions in the Americas, EMEA, and APAC. The team owns regional go-to-market strategy and execution — high-touch account-based marketing, field programs, third-party conferences, executive engagement, and partner-led motions — and works cross-functionally with Sales, Product Marketing, Events, Brand, and Demand to drive customer acquisition and expansion across enterprise and AI-native accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Director of EMEA Field Marketing&lt;/strong&gt; to own the customer engagement and pipeline-generation strategy and execution across EMEA, and to establish CoreWeave as a recognized and trusted brand in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will lead and grow a team of regional marketing managers, and partner closely with sales leadership to align marketing investments and resourcing around the GEO go-to-market strategy supporting customer acquisition and customer expansion across enterprise and AI-natives. As leader of Field Marketing for EMEA, you will play a pivotal role in shaping and executing our regional marketing strategy across high-touch account-based marketing, 3rd party conferences, field programs, executive engagement, and partner-led motions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will own how CoreWeave shows up in the region — building awareness and credibility with European AI-native builders and enterprise buyers, and adapting the global brand narrative for a market with distinct data sovereignty, regulatory, language, and cultural requirements. Your leadership will drive the expansion of CoreWeave&#39;s presence and reputation in the dynamic and rapidly evolving EMEA AI-Cloud market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success is measured by pipeline created and progressed, conversion rates across the funnel, deal velocity in priority accounts, and growth in regional brand awareness and consideration among target accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Strategy &amp;amp; Pipeline Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the EMEA customer engagement and pipeline-generation strategy end to end, carrying accountability for sourced and influenced pipeline targets by segment, country, and priority account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align marketing investment and team resourcing to the GEO go-to-market strategy, ensuring the regional plan reflects where Sales is prioritizing acquisition and expansion across enterprise and AI-native accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance investment between near-term pipeline generation and the brand and category-building work required to make CoreWeave a known quantity in EMEA, and be able to articulate the tradeoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the channel mix across ABM, field programs, third-party conferences, executive engagement, and partner-led motions based on ROI analysis and attribution data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build distinct motions for acquisition and expansion: net-new account penetration and category presence on one side, deeper multi-workload engagement within existing customers on the other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize across a multi-country region — sequencing investment across core markets and emerging ones rather than spreading coverage thin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a multi-million dollar regional budget with explicit ROI rationale, and defend allocation and resourcing decisions to marketing and sales leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand Presence &amp;amp; Market Development in EMEA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own CoreWeave&#39;s overall brand presence in EMEA — partnering with the Brand, Communications, and Product Marketing teams to build awareness, credibility, and consideration in a market where CoreWeave is still establishing itself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt the global brand narrative for regional realities: data sovereignty and residency, EU regulatory context, local infrastructure footprint, language and cultural nuance — without fragmenting the global story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Land regional proof points — customer stories, local infrastructure milestones, partner wins — and make them visible in-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Partnership &amp;amp; Account-Based Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the senior marketing partner to EMEA sales leadership — in pipeline reviews, account planning, and forecast discussions — translating GEO priorities into funded, resourced programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct high-touch ABM against CoreWeave&#39;s priority AI-native and enterprise accounts, partnering with Sales to define coverage, nomination criteria, and progression goals at the account and contact level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive disciplined lead and opportunity handoff with Sales and SDR, with agreed SLAs, shared quality definitions, and acceleration plays for stalled or late-stage deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build expansion programs alongside Sales and Customer teams that deepen engagement in existing accounts and surface new workloads, teams, and buying centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Presence &amp;amp; Executive Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand CoreWeave&#39;s presence across the EMEA AI-Cloud market, selecting the third-party conferences, field programs, and technical and developer-led moments where CoreWeave should show up — and holding each to a pipeline and brand thesis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Executive Marketing team to connect regional CXO and VP engagement to opportunity progression in named accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Partner Marketing to activate partner-led motions in-region — including the regional systems integrators, resellers, and cloud and ecosystem partners that carry disproportionate weight in EMEA — turning joint narratives into named-account plays and co-sell pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear regional input into global campaigns and launches so they land effectively with EMEA audiences and buyer personas, and flag where regional adaptation is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Developer Marketing to grow developer advocacy and engagement with in EMEA communities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Optimization &amp;amp; Scalable Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the KPIs that matter — account and contact coverage, engagement, meetings, sourced and influenced pipeline, conversion rates and stage progression — in Salesforce and the marketing automation and ABM stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish testing and optimization frameworks across messaging, audience, channel, and offer: hypothesis, test, measure, then scale or retire.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the repeatable systems that make regional growth predictable — program briefs and business cases, target account and contact selection, program templates, and playbooks any country team can run.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing Operations and Revenue Operations on attribution, lead scoring, and reporting so regional investment ties cleanly to revenue outcomes, and deliver post-program reporting that drives explicit go/no-go decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within EMEA data privacy and consent requirements (GDPR and local equivalents), partnering with Legal and Marketing Ops to keep regional data practices compliant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of regional marketing managers, hiring to plan as the EMEA team scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a team of pipeline-focused field marketers who understand the full customer journey, the sales process, and their own revenue impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear ownership boundaries and escalation paths so the team coordinates with Events, Brand, Partner Marketing, and Demand Gen rather than absorbing their scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent EMEA performance and plans in global marketing forums, and partner with Americas and APAC counterparts on global initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced regional marketing leader:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years in B2B marketing at high-growth technology or enterprise companies, with direct pipeline accountability across field marketing, demand generation, or ABM supporting EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People leader:&lt;/strong&gt; 4+ years leading regional or field marketing teams with pipeline accountability, including hiring and developing marketers across a distributed, multi-country geography.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand builder in-region:&lt;/strong&gt; Track record establishing or scaling a brand in EMEA for a company earlier in its regional journey — building awareness and credibility from a low base, and adapting a global narrative to local market realities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EMEA market fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of the region&#39;s diversity — buying behavior, language and cultural differences, data sovereignty and regulatory considerations, and the partner and ecosystem landscape across core and emerging markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales-aligned operator:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience partnering directly with executive sales leadership to shape GEO go-to-market plans, and allocating marketing investment and headcount against territory and account priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account- and deal-centric:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong grasp of complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise personas and how ABM, executive engagement, and field programs influence acquisition, expansion, and close rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data and analytics depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Advanced proficiency with pipeline attribution, conversion analysis, and ROI optimization using Salesforce, Tableau and ABM platforms, and BI tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program range:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to build across the full regional mix — ABM, third-party conferences, field programs, executive experiences, brand and community moments, and partner co-marketing — with clear evidence of impact from each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-curious:&lt;/strong&gt; Genuinely interested in AI infrastructure and how AI-native and enterprise customers build and scale workloads, with the ability to ramp quickly on CoreWeave&#39;s platform and market to CTOs, CIOs, VPs of Engineering, and AI/ML leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel across the region as programs require.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;CoreWeave does not accept speculative CVs. Any unsolicited CVs received will be treated as the property of CoreWeave and your Terms &amp;amp; Conditions associated with the use of CVs will be considered null and void.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Any unsolicited CVs sent by your company to us – that is to say, in any situation where we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy – will be considered by us to be a “free gift”, leaving us liable for no fees whatsoever should we choose to contact the candidate directly and engage the candidate’s services, and will in no way establish any prior claim by your company to representation of that candidate should the candidate’s details also be submitted by any other party.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires access to export controlled information. &amp;nbsp;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations applicable to that information, applicant must either be (A) a U.S. person, defined as a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful permanent resident (green card holder), (iii) refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, (B) eligible to access the export controlled information without a required export authorization, or (C) eligible and reasonably likely to obtain the required export authorization from the applicable U.S. government agency. &amp;nbsp;CoreWeave may, for legitimate business reasons, decline to pursue any export licensing process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Updated privacy notice - UK and EU Job Applications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected by CoreWeave UK Ltd. (“Controller”), which is located at&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Phosphor (6th Floor), 133 Park Street, London, SE1 9EA&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;and can be contacted by emailing ----- Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at ----- Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of (i) Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) and (ii) the GDPR as it forms part of the laws of the UK (“UK GDPR”), as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment. Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. With respect to transfers originating from the UK or the European Economic Area (&quot;EEA&quot;) to a country outside the UK or the EEA, we implement the appropriate transfer mechanism(s) and other appropriate solutions to address cross-border transfers as required by applicable law. You may request a copy of the suitable mechanisms we have in place by contacting us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. Where permitted by applicable law, we may also retain your personal data for a limited period after the recruitment process ends in order to consider you for future job opportunities, respond to legal claims, or comply with record-keeping obligations. Under the GDPR and the UK GDPR, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability. In addition, you may lodge a complaint with the relevant supervisory authority: (i) A list of Europe’s data protection authorities can be found &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/structure/data-protection-authorities/index_en.htm__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9xVQGfFw$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;; and (ii) for the UK, this is the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ico.org.uk/__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9IDhJOUA$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Information Commissioner&#39;s Office&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For additional information, please see our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.coreweave.com/docs/policies/terms-of-service/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;description content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/&quot;&gt;Thoughtworks&lt;/a&gt; is a global technology consultancy that integrates design, engineering and AI to drive digital innovation. We are over 10,000 people strong across 47 offices in 18 countries. For 30+ years, we’ve delivered extraordinary impact together with our clients by helping them solve complex business problems with technology and culture as the differentiator.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Thoughtworks.com is one of our most important customer-facing products, helping clients discover our expertise, explore evidence of our impact and take the next step with us. It also helps job seekers explore opportunities and gives search engines and AI assistants an accurate, trusted understanding of who we are and what we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, fragmented ownership across Marketing limits our ability to deliver connected customer journeys, maintain consistent quality and continuously improve performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Head of Product Design to change that. You’ll lead Thoughtworks.com as a digital product, translating our go-to-market and employer brand strategies into seamless experiences for customers, job seekers and AI agents. You’ll own the website strategy, roadmap, customer journeys, publishing model and content and design quality. You&#39;ll also shape experiences across connected channels, including email through Knak and events through Splash, while influencing the internal workflows that drive quality, consistency and speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, player-coach role for someone who can think strategically and deliver at every level, from defining roadmaps and improving customer journeys to refining copy, reviewing designs, interpreting performance data and making launch decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-responsibilities&quot;&gt;Job responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-responsibilities content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Website product strategy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the product vision, principles and roadmap for Thoughtworks.com&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize work around customer and business outcomes rather than requests for individual pages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect the website roadmap to Thoughtworks’ go-to-market priorities, propositions and major company launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer journeys and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a deep understanding of our audiences, including enterprise buyers, technology leaders, practitioners, partners, prospective employees and alumni community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design connected journeys that help people move from a question/problem/need to relevant services, expertise, evidence and action, where the site fuels journeys on AI platforms that might never have users interact with our site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer research, website data and market insight to identify friction and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the core website, event pages and email experiences work together where they form part of the same journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Narrative, copy and content quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the quality and coherence of the website narrative, copy and information architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technology services and Thoughtworks expertise into clear, credible experiences for different audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge unclear propositions, duplicated content, unsupported claims and pages that do not serve a defined customer need&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the central Content team, service-line marketers and subject-matter experts, while keeping accountability for how content works within the overall experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with content operations to establish reusable content patterns, editorial standards and clear ownership for maintaining important content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experiences for people and agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the website is useful and understandable to human visitors, search engines and AI assistants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the SEO and LLM Discoverability Lead to improve how Thoughtworks is found, interpreted and represented to support buyers in their decision making process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape requirements for structured content, metadata, evidence, content relationships and reusable information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance machine readability with strong human storytelling, accessibility and brand expression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Publishing model for the AI era&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the spec for redesigning the publishing workflow from brief through design, production, approval, release and ongoing improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the GTM tech and Global IT teams to replace manual, error-prone production with reusable patterns, clearer decision rights and proportionate automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify where AI can improve research, prototyping, content preparation, metadata, accessibility checks, quality assurance and content maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn good judgment into practical standards, templates, playbooks and automated checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a model that allows teams to move faster without lowering the quality bar or creating uncontrolled publishing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design quality and experimentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the direction and quality bar for UX, UI, interaction design and the website design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use qualitative and quantitative evidence to improve journeys, messaging and conversion over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sign off on experience quality before major launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and agency leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a multidisciplinary team spanning product design, experience production, transformation and discoverability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give people clear outcomes, decision rights, constructive feedback and room to do excellent work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an effective working model with the central Content team, GTM technology, Global IT and service-line marketers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-qualifications&quot;&gt;Job qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-qualifications content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;technical-skills&quot;&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;qualifications inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 - 15 years experience leading digital products, customer experiences, service design or product design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong record of turning customer insight and business strategy into coherent end-to-end experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment across product, UX, content and design, with the ability to recognize and explain what good looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing and editorial instincts, including the confidence to simplify complex ideas and challenge unclear copy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with marketing, product, design, engineering and senior business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial understanding and the ability to connect digital experience decisions to go-to-market outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinking, including experience creating reusable patterns, design systems, operating models or publishing frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of search, structured content and how AI assistants discover and interpret information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to improve how work is researched, designed, produced or assured&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to operate in ambiguity, make difficult prioritization decisions and move from strategy to delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of leading and coaching people or multidisciplinary teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;professional-skills&quot;&gt;Professional Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;skills inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a natural ability to establish and nurture relationships with senior leaders across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent context-switching capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in situations where you are given little to no direction and have the ability to lead, organize and deliver commitments on time and within budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re resilient in ambiguous situations and can adapt your role to approach challenges from multiple perspectives. You don’t shy away from risks, instead you take them on and skillfully manage them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re empathetic and use this ability to build solid working relationships and resolve issues quickly and thoughtfully&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;important-things&quot;&gt;Other things to know&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;important-things content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is no one-size-fits-all career path at Thoughtworks: however you want to develop your career is entirely up to you. But we also balance autonomy with the strength of our cultivation culture. This means your career is supported by interactive tools, numerous development programs and teammates who want to help you grow. We see value in helping each other be our best and that extends to empowering our employees in their career journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;responsible-ai-use&quot;&gt;Responsible Use of AI in Recruitment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;responsible-ai-use content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Thoughtworks, we use AI tools to support our recruitment team with administrative tasks such as drafting communications, scheduling interviews and writing job descriptions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Crucially, our AI tools do not screen, assess, rank or make hiring decisions. Every application is reviewed by our team and all selection decisions are made exclusively by our interviewers and hiring managers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to fairness and responsible AI. We actively manage our AI systems by testing, monitoring for biased outcomes and implementing mitigation measures. We hold our third-party vendors to these same high standards through a rigorous governance process. For additional information, please see our full &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/careers/ai-policy-for-recruitment&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Thoughtworks AI Policy for Recruitment&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about&quot;&gt;About Thoughtworks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;about content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thoughtworks is a dynamic and inclusive community of bright and supportive colleagues who are revolutionizing tech. As a leading technology consultancy, we’re pushing boundaries through our purposeful and impactful work. For 30+ years, we’ve delivered extraordinary impact together with our clients by helping them solve complex business problems with technology as the differentiator. Bring your brilliant expertise and commitment for continuous learning to Thoughtworks. Together, let’s be extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;display: none;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/careers/ai-policy-for-recruitment&quot;&gt;See here our AI policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Artefact is an AI-native company fusing engineering-grade delivery with strategic consulting to drive high-impact results. We specialize in accelerating end-to-end data and AI transformation, helping enterprises turn marketing into a predictable engine for business growth across the value chain. From strategy to implementation, Artefact delivers bespoke, scalable AI solutions tailored to our clients&#39; core business challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Paris, Artefact operates across 27 countries with a global team of over 2,500 employees, partnering with leading international brands across luxury, retail, FMCG, industry, healthcare, and finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To support our rapid expansion, we are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Chief of Staff to the Group CMO (Intern)&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Global Marketing team starting in &lt;strong&gt;January 2027&lt;/strong&gt; for a minimum of 6 months.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you passionate about B2B marketing, tech innovation, and generative AI? Do you want to work in an environment where your contributions directly accelerate business growth?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Chief of Staff to the Group CMO (Intern)&lt;/strong&gt;, you will play a central role in driving Artefact’s flagship initiative: &lt;strong&gt;&quot;AI-Augmented Marketing&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;. This global project reshapes how our international marketing teams operate by embedding analytical rigor, agentic AI workflows, and operational excellence into everyday execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working directly alongside the Group CMO, you will collaborate closely with regional marketing teams, data scientists, and business analysts worldwide. Fluency in English is essential, as you will lead international workshops, align stakeholders, and scale best practices across all Artefact entities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic orchestration:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Group CMO in executing the global &lt;em&gt;AI-Augmented Marketing&lt;/em&gt; roadmap across three core pillars :&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Derive actionable insights from the marketing data platform to guide executive decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agentic content workflows:&lt;/strong&gt; Automate content operations by building and deploying an AI skill/agent library using tools such as Gemini Enterprise, Claude, and Lovable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Scale adoption across international hubs by designing learning modules, documenting playbooks, and running hands-on training sessions in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-to-market &amp;amp; revenue operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Leverage AI tools and skills to optimize inbound and outbound funnels, drive pipeline velocity, and enhance Marketing-Sales alignment for sustained lead generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance measurement &amp;amp; reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Build, maintain, and optimize full-funnel B2B performance dashboards (awareness, activation, ABM) to measure campaign ROI and surface continuous improvement opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Own and update cross-functional tracking tools, operational dashboards, and meeting cadences to maintain project momentum and organizational alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-impact copywriting &amp;amp; editorial:&lt;/strong&gt; Produce high-converting editorial assets (internal/external newsletters, landing pages, case studies, and thought leadership articles) while safeguarding brand tone and positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Profile &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Master’s student from a top-tier Business School (&lt;em&gt;Grande École de Commerce&lt;/em&gt;) or equivalent university program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong data-driven problem-solving abilities; comfortable working with analytics platforms, data modeling, and reporting frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Tech native:&lt;/strong&gt; A genuine passion for emerging technologies, generative &amp;amp; agentic AI tools, and B2B growth marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; copywriting:&lt;/strong&gt; Bilingual or fluent in English (both written and spoken) with exceptional writing skills across long-form, web, and newsletter formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project management:&lt;/strong&gt; High organizational agility, rigorous attention to detail, and the ability to prioritize competing deadlines in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactive, autonomous, results-oriented, and excited to collaborate with cross-functional, international teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start date:&lt;/strong&gt; January 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duration:&lt;/strong&gt; 6 months minimum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Paris Headquarters (with hybrid flexibility)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary&lt;/strong&gt; : 1200€&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt; High potential for conversion into a permanent contract (CDI) based on mutual fit and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Artefact is an equal opportunity employer. We recruit solely based on merit and business needs, fostering an inclusive environment free from discrimination of any kind.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pilotez les missions où se jouent les paris IA des grands groupes, et transformez-les en résultats mesurables&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;L’IA, et en particulier l’IA agentique, figure parmi les priorités des comités de direction. Chez Artefact, nous sommes des makers. “We Make AI Work” : notre métier n’est pas de commenter l’IA, c’est de la faire fonctionner, à grande échelle, au cœur des grands groupes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Et tout commence par vous.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Missions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant qu’&lt;strong&gt;AI Strategist Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, vous construisez avec les dirigeants de nos clients une stratégie IA crédible, un modèle opératoire adapté et un programme de transformation qui génère une valeur mesurable. Vous êtes le moteur de nos missions AI Strategy : vous les pilotez en autonomie, en garantissez la qualité, les délais et la rentabilité, faites grandir les consultants qui y sont staffés et développez vos comptes aux côtés des Directeurs et Partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous commencez là où débute toute transformation IA : par l’ambition du client, son secteur d’activité et ses processus métier, et non par la technologie. Et vous restez un maker : vous ne vous arrêtez pas au slide. Vous construisez vous-même analyses, business cases et démos fonctionnelles (vibe coding, low-code, no-code) que le client peut toucher, et vous développez un domaine d’expertise solide dans un secteur ou une fonction métier.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous travaillez main dans la main avec nos équipes Engineering (qui construisent et livrent des solutions d’IA agentique) et nos équipes AI Adoption (qui favorisent leur adoption) : vous définissez les processus cibles et la roadmap, Engineering les construit et les livre, et AI Adoption accompagne les personnes dans le changement, dès le premier jour.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activités &amp;amp; Responsabilités&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;I. Conception de la stratégie et de la transformation IA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous définissez la vision IA et la roadmap priorisée des cas d’usage, challengez la pertinence de l’IA et assumez les arbitrages. Lorsque c’est pertinent, vous conduisez des refontes de processus de bout en bout, en pensant lean avant de déployer l’IA et en mobilisant les équipes Engineering et AI Adoption pour les livrer. Vous concevez le modèle opératoire cible et sécurisez ses conditions de succès.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;II. Analyses, business cases &amp;amp; prototypage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous concevez et pilotez les travaux d’analyse de la mission, business cases inclus, afin de sécuriser des décisions fondées sur les données et sur les faits, et vous revoyez le travail de l’équipe. Vous prototypez rapidement des cas d’usage pour illustrer la valeur par la démo et aider les clients à se projeter dans la solution finale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;III. Delivery, livrables &amp;amp; collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous dirigez les missions au quotidien en donnant de la visibilité aux sponsors clients : vous découpez chaque mission en streams, anticipez les risques et challengez le client lorsque c’est pertinent. Vous produisez en autonomie des livrables de niveau C-suite et des synthèses exécutives, structurez la storyline et veillez au respect des standards de qualité Artefact. Vous orchestrez les équipes Engineering pour la faisabilité technique et les équipes AI Adoption pour ancrer l’adoption sur le terrain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IV. Relation client &amp;amp; développement commercial&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous êtes l’interlocuteur de confiance des directeurs métiers et des responsables de projets (Comex-1) : vous cartographiez les rapports de force entre les parties prenantes, animez les restitutions pour emporter l’adhésion et maximiser le NPS client, et gérez les tensions et escalades en préservant la confiance. Vous détectez de nouveaux besoins sur le terrain, construisez le plan de développement du compte avec le Directeur ou le Partner et déclenchez de manière proactive des propositions pour développer les comptes existants, en contribuant aux propositions commerciales et aux soutenances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;V. Équipe &amp;amp; connaissances&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous encadrez et faites grandir les consultants juniors et seniors, êtes counsellor de plusieurs collègues et participez au recrutement des futurs talents. Vous contribuez aussi à la base de connaissances interne par des articles et des retours d’expérience, et animez des formations internes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profil recherché&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vous vous reconnaissez si&lt;/strong&gt;… vous aimez piloter des missions exigeantes de bout en bout, faire grandir une équipe et gagner la confiance de dirigeants, et si vous préférez mettre une démo entre leurs mains plutôt que leur décrire une vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 à 8 ans d’expérience au sein d’un cabinet de conseil en stratégie, en management ou en transformation data / IA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une formation supérieure de niveau licence ou master, issue d’un cursus académique d’excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience de pilotage de missions complexes, de la vision aux résultats, avec des business cases qui résistent à l’examen d’un Comex.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une solide compréhension des enjeux opérationnels de l’IA (IA générative et agentique, gouvernance, cas d’usage métiers), avec la capacité de l’expliquer simplement à des dirigeants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience de pilotage de projets de refonte de processus métier, avec une maîtrise avérée de certains processus métier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience du développement commercial (propositions, développement de comptes, relation avec des décideurs de haut niveau).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience d’encadrement d’une équipe de consultants, avec le goût de faire grandir, de déléguer et de tirer l’équipe vers le haut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un état d’esprit de maker : aisance avec les outils technologiques actuels et capacité à prototyper rapidement des démos fonctionnelles (low-code, no-code, outils agentiques) qui rendent la valeur tangible pour le client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise parfaite du français et de l’anglais (oral et écrit).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;À propos d’Artefact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact est un cabinet de conseil spécialisé en data et en intelligence artificielle, qui accompagne les entreprises pour transformer ces technologies en impact business concret et mesurable. À la croisée du conseil, de la data et de la technologie, nos 2 500 collaborateurs dans 27 pays mettent leurs expertises en commun pour concevoir, développer et déployer des solutions qui répondent aux enjeux de transformation de nos clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre accompagnement couvre l’intégralité de la chaîne de valeur : &lt;strong&gt;AI Strategy&lt;/strong&gt; (cadrage stratégique, opportunités à fort impact, trajectoires, modèles opératoires), &lt;strong&gt;Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; (industrialisation, architectures agentiques, produits data) et &lt;strong&gt;AI Adoption&lt;/strong&gt; (conduite du changement, montée en compétences, usage quotidien de l’IA).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pour en savoir plus sur Artefact, nos expertises et notre culture : &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.artefact.com&quot;&gt;https://www.artefact.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi nous rejoindre ?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;De la stratégie à la réalisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Ne pas s’arrêter aux recommandations : participer à la conception et à la concrétisation de solutions IA répondant à de véritables enjeux métiers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une collaboration entre expertises&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Occuper un rôle à la croisée de la stratégie (AI Strategy), de la technologie (Engineering) et de l&#39;humain (AI Adoption).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Piloter ce qui compte&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Des missions de transformation IA de bout en bout, au cœur des enjeux des grands groupes, avec une vraie autonomie, une équipe à faire grandir et des comptes à développer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une trajectoire qui accélère &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Un parcours clair vers Senior Manager puis Directeur, dans un environnement d’apprentissage continu axé sur la transmission des connaissances et le pragmatisme technologique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processus de recrutement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;entretien de fit RH&lt;/strong&gt; (45&#39;) avec HR / Talent Acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;business case AI-driven&lt;/strong&gt; (60&#39;) avec un AI Strategist Senior Manager ou Directeur&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;business case de prototypage IA hands-on&lt;/strong&gt; (60&#39;) avec un AI Strategist Senior Manager ou Directeur&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;jeu de rôle AI Strategist Manager&lt;/strong&gt; (45&#39;-60&#39;) avec un AI Strategist Directeur ou Partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un &lt;strong&gt;entretien de fit final&lt;/strong&gt; (30&#39;) avec un AI Strategist Partner ou Managing Partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération : 66 000€ à 75 000€ brut annuel (fixe) + 10 000€ de variable, selon expérience et séniorité&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Artefact, nous sommes convaincus que la diversité des parcours, des expériences et des perspectives fait la richesse de nos équipes. Nous nous engageons à offrir un environnement inclusif et des opportunités équitables, où chacune et chacun peut évoluer et exprimer pleinement son potentiel. Nos recrutements reposent sur les compétences, le potentiel et l’adéquation avec le rôle.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrated Marketing France connects global marketing strategy with local business priorities to deliver impactful marketing campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As Senior Marketing Manager, Integrated Marketing, you will identify France’s priority marketing moments and translate global direction into a clear, integrated marketing plan. Using business performance, consumer insights and knowledge of the French market, you will recommend what to prioritise, what to adopt from global campaigns and what to adapt to maximise local impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will bring teams together around clear priorities, challenge recommendations constructively, simplify complex topics and ensure marketing initiatives deliver against France’s business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Marketing Strategy &amp;amp; Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse business performance, consumer insights and market trends to recommend France’s priority marketing moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate global marketing direction into an integrated France marketing plan, identifying what to adopt, adapt or challenge based on local business needs and market specificities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear, evidence-based recommendations on priorities and trade-offs, balancing expected impact, investment and available resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong rationale for local adaptations and influence global stakeholders when the French market requires a different approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Campaign Orchestration &amp;amp; Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead campaign kick-offs and align local and global stakeholders around clear objectives, responsibilities and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge functional recommendations constructively, asking the right questions to ensure proposed media plans, creative concepts and campaign choices meet France’s objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simplify complex, cross-functional topics, clarify dependencies and facilitate decisions to keep initiatives moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate delivery risks, resolve coordination challenges and ensure campaigns are delivered on time and to the agreed brief.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Marketing Plan Consolidation &amp;amp; Executive Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidate the France marketing plan into a clear, executive-level overview of key priorities, campaign choices, local adaptations and expected business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write concise, insight-led strategic memos articulating the rationale behind France’s marketing recommendations, key trade-offs and decisions requiring alignment or approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a compelling, evidence-based narrative connecting France’s business priorities and market specificities with global marketing strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present and defend France’s marketing recommendations to global executives, ensuring local choices are understood and enabling informed decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years of experience&lt;/strong&gt; in integrated marketing, marketing strategy, campaign planning or marketing programme management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen, analytical thinking and the ability to translate data and consumer insights into actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong critical thinking and sound judgement: able to challenge assumptions, ask the right questions and assess whether proposed marketing choices support business objectives, without needing to be the technical expert in every discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance global consistency with relevant local adaptation, using clear evidence and constructive influencing skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to simplify complex topics and align teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational skills, pragmatism and ownership, with a focus on prioritisation and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in French and English, with the confidence to challenge and influence stakeholders in an international environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success Measures&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear, business-led recommendation of France’s priority marketing moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant local adaptations of global campaigns, supported by clear rationale and market insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong alignment across stakeholders on priorities, decisions and delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Campaigns delivered on time and against agreed objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, actionable performance insights and executive visibility on the France marketing plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DASH Brands will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about DASH Brands&#39; legitimate recruiting process at&lt;/em&gt; &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _2rkolb4i _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-is-router-link=&quot;false&quot; data-testid=&quot;link-with-safety&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi Deliveroo ?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lorsque l&#39;on vous dit Deliveroo, vous imaginez sans doute d&#39;abord les bons petits plats livrés chez vous en moins d&#39;une demi-heure. Plutôt sympa non ? Mais c&#39;est en coulisses que l&#39;histoire est la plus intéressante. Nous opérons désormais à travers le monde et travaillons avec plus de 176 000 restaurants partenaires et commerces en tous genres en France. Nous collaborons avec des milliers de livreurs et de livreuses partenaires pour le plus grand bonheur de nos millions de personnes clientes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous recherchons un·e Assistant·e Chef de Projet Marketing Merchant en alternance pour rejoindre notre équipe Marketing à Paris, pour une durée de 12 mois. Aux côtés de l&#39;équipe Merchant, vous contribuerez au développement de la croissance de nos partenaires, au déploiement de nos campagnes nationales 360° et en accompagnerez des projets à fort impact sur l&#39;acquisition, la rétention et la fidélisation de nos restaurants partenaires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Descriptif du poste :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant qu’Apprenti(e) dans l’équipe Marketing Merchant Restaurant, vous travaillerez au quotidien avec l&#39;équipe marketing chargée de mettre en avant toute la sélection de restaurants et de partenaires de Deliveroo. Vous serez également amené(e) à &lt;strong&gt;interagir régulièrement avec les autres départements marketing &lt;/strong&gt;tels que l’équipe média, l’équipe créative, le CRM ainsi qu’avec l’&lt;strong&gt;équipe commerciale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos missions consisteront à:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mettre en avant sur l’application les restaurants et partenaires disponibles sur l’app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soutenir l’équipe commerciale dans la création et l’exécution de plans marketing destinés à mettre en avant les partenaires présents sur Deliveroo.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborer étroitement avec l&#39;équipe commerciale et les équipes marketing transversales (marque, réseaux sociaux, CRM et influenceurs) pour développer et exécuter des plans partenaires basés sur les priorités commerciales (par exemple, objectifs régionaux, accords d&#39;exclusivité, renégociations).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Préparer des présentations et des supports pour appuyer les discussions de l&#39;équipe commerciale avec les partenaires, en veillant à l&#39;alignement et à la clarté.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer à l’exécution des points forts des partenaires en collaboration avec le CRM et le Commercial (communications mensuelles d&#39;exclusivité / bannières dédiées sur l’application / notifications push...).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gérer le budget alloué pour le plan de chaque partenaire, en optimisant les ressources locales pour obtenir un impact maximal.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyser l’impact de nos campagnes pour en tirer des recommandations pour les équipes commerciales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cette alternance vous permettra d&#39;appréhender de nombreux sujets marketing (création de campagne, analyse, sensibilité client) et vous permettra d&#39;acquérir une bonne connaissance des enjeux marketing et de la gestion de projets complexes grâce à la collaboration transverse que vous aurez avec les autres pôles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ce qui vous permettra de réussir&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous préparez un diplôme de niveau Bac+4 ou Bac+5 en école de commerce, université ou équivalent, avec une spécialisation en marketing, communication ou digital et recherchez une alternance d&#39;une durée d&#39;un an à partir de Décembre 2026 / Janvier 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vous Vous Reconnaissez Dans Les Points Suivants&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous êtes organisé·e, rigoureux·se et savez gérer plusieurs projets en parallèle en respectant les délais&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous avez une excellente communication écrite et orale en français ainsi qu&#39;un bon niveau d&#39;anglais.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous êtes à l&#39;aise avec les chiffres et aimez analyser les performances pour en tirer des recommandations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous appréciez le travail en équipe et la coordination de nombreux interlocuteurs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous êtes curieux·se, proactif·ve et souhaitez évoluer dans un environnement dynamique et en forte croissance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Voici un&lt;a href=&quot;https://sites.google.com/deliveroo.co.uk/biz-interview-guide/home?authuser=0&quot;&gt; lien&lt;/a&gt; avec de la documentation pour vous préparer aux entretiens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous offrons un environnement de travail dynamique et stimulant, où vous aurez l&#39;opportunité de développer vos compétences et de contribuer activement à notre mission. Rejoignez notre équipe exceptionnelle dès maintenant et faites partie de cette aventure passionnante !&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;La vie chez Deliveroo :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre équipe est en forte croissance, notre impact très important, et nous cherchons à répondre aux questions les plus stimulantes du moment. Nous progressons rapidement, nous explorons toujours de nouvelles idées et nous sommes très transparents quant aux décisions que nous prenons et à ce qui motive nos choix.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Il y a tellement de questions que nous souhaitons résoudre, et encore plus que nous n&#39;avons pas encore rencontrées. Comment les données et la technologie peuvent-elles aider les restaurants à développer leur activité à mesure que les habitudes des consommateurs évoluent ? Comment pouvons-nous prédire ce qu&#39;une personne souhaitera pour dîner avant même que l&#39;idée ne lui vienne à l&#39;esprit ? Chez Deliveroo, ces questions ne sont que quelques-uns des défis ambitieux auxquels nous nous efforçons de répondre – et il n&#39;y a aucun projet qui ne peut pas devenir le vôtre. Aucune solution n&#39;appartient à une équipe en particulier, ce qui vous ouvre d&#39;extraordinaires possibilités en termes de développement et d&#39;impact personnel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;À compétences égales, ce poste est ouvert aux travailleurs et travailleuses en situation de handicap ou assimilés au sens de l’article L5212-13 du Code du travail. Deliveroo s’engage en faveur de la diversité, l’égalité professionnelle, l’emploi des personnes en situation de handicap.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DASH Brands will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about DASH Brands&#39; legitimate recruiting process at&lt;/em&gt; &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _2rkolb4i _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-is-router-link=&quot;false&quot; data-testid=&quot;link-with-safety&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Dashlane&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left: 0.0in;&quot;&gt;Dashlane’s mission is to deliver the credential security every business and employee needs to thrive. Millions of consumers, and over 25,000 brands worldwide, such as Michelin, Air France, and Forrester, trust Dashlane for industry-leading innovations, patented zero-knowledge security, and an unmatched user experience. Founded in Paris, Dashlane has since established offices in New York and Lisbon, and has grown to more than 300 Dashlaners globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left: 0.0in;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for people who actively use AI tools to drive efficiency, creativity, and impact in their work. At Dashlane, we drive innovation and value learning, strive for excellence in everything we do, and thrive as one team. Learn more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://lifeatdashlane.com/&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;link&quot;&gt;&lt;u data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;life at Dashlane&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, including &lt;a href=&quot;https://lifeatdashlane.com/how-we-work&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;link&quot;&gt;&lt;u data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;how we work&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://lifeatdashlane.com/how-we-hire&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;link&quot;&gt;&lt;u data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;how we hire&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, and the &lt;a href=&quot;https://lifeatdashlane.com/benefits-dashlane&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;link&quot;&gt;&lt;u data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;benefits of being a Dashlaner&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left: 0.0in;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;4930fb65-d24c-4176-8ea9-6cb03614cd29&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot; data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;strong&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;fabric-text-color-mark&quot; data-text-custom-color=&quot;#000000&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;mark&quot; data-prosemirror-mark-name=&quot;textColor&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;4c53fb95&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The Sharing &amp;amp; Vault team is responsible for how people securely store and share credentials. The team works on sensitive product surfaces at the heart of credential security, balancing strong zero-knowledge principles with simple, reliable experiences for users and admins.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;36409253&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;As a senior web engineer, you will shape intuitive, trustworthy interfaces and the client-side foundations behind them, turning security requirements into polished product experiences that are scalable, accessible, and easy to use. You will own complex features from design to production, mentor teammates, and help shape the team&#39;s technical direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;legacy-color-text-default&quot;&gt;Location-Specific Information:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be based in Paris, with English as your working language. At Dashlane, we embrace a hybrid culture that combines the best of both worlds: the creativity and energy of in-person collaboration with the flexibility of remote work. Our model is designed to strengthen team connections while supporting individual productivity and work-life balance. To maximize collaboration, we come together in the office on Mondays, Tuesdays, and Thursdays, while Wednesdays and Fridays offer more flexibility for focused work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-local-id=&quot;7191c8df4d17&quot; data-prosemirror-content-type=&quot;node&quot; data-prosemirror-node-name=&quot;paragraph&quot; data-prosemirror-node-block=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
